# Trivy ignore list for go-libsignal.
#
# The gate is a SOURCE filesystem scan (trivy fs) of the shipped Go module,
# failing on CRITICAL/HIGH (conventions/devops.md §8). tests/, examples/ and
# bench/ are skipped: none of them ship to a consumer, and tests/interop/rust
# carries the upstream Rust reference crate purely to diff wire bytes against.
#
# There is no image gate yet. The only container this repo builds is the
# Rust<->Go interop harness, and tests/interop/Dockerfile does not build
# today — the crate's Cargo.toml has path dependencies on a sibling upstream
# libsignal checkout the Dockerfile never provides. `make trivy-image` carries
# the ready-to-use scan; wire it into `make security` and add the CI job once
# the Dockerfile is repaired.
#
# Add specific advisory IDs below ONLY when a finding is confirmed
# not-applicable or unfixable, with a one-line justification AND the date it
# was accepted. An entry without both is a defect.
#
# Example:
# CVE-XXXX-XXXXX  # 2026-01-01 <reason this advisory does not apply here>
